# Crow: a crow-gateway.service drop-in that gives the gateway the reports door
# socket. Installed as
#   /etc/systemd/system/crow-gateway.service.d/report-readers.conf
#
# WHY A DROP-IN AND NOT THE SHIPPED UNIT: the gateway's own unit is the installer's
# (scripts/crow-install.sh) and an owner may edit it; a drop-in adds the lines this
# feature needs without rewriting their file, the same way the proxy socket's drop-in
# does. Everything this file does not name stays exactly as the unit has it,
# WorkingDirectory included.
#
# WHY Wants=/After= AND NOT Requires=: the gateway must be able to start whether or
# not the door socket exists — that is what keeps a gateway restartable for its own
# reasons while the socket is missing or broken, and the listener answers its 503
# "this link doesn't open a report" page until the socket is back. After= is what
# makes the socket be started first, so the fd exists before the process that needs it.
#
# WHY Sockets= NAMES ONLY THIS ONE UNIT: a Sockets= line in a drop-in APPENDS to the
# list, it does not replace it, so the Caddy proxy socket's own drop-in keeps that
# unit in place and this line adds the door beside it. That is also why the proxy
# socket unit is deliberately NOT repeated here: a second mention would hand the same
# fd over twice.
#
# WHY ExecStart IS RESET AND RE-STATED: systemd hands socket-activation fds to the
# MAIN PID and to no other process, and pickActivatedFd refuses a LISTEN_PID that is
# not this process's own (servers/gateway/proxy-socket.js). The installer's ExecStart
# is `ExecStart=$(which node) servers/gateway/index.js` — systemd execs that directly,
# with no shell in between, so a plain node unit is already the MainPID. A unit
# written as `npm run gateway` is the one that needs this: there npm is the MainPID
# and node the gateway runs in is npm's CHILD, which inherits neither the fd's
# LISTEN_PID nor the argv the fd was meant for, so the gateway would refuse the
# socket. An empty ExecStart= clears the inherited value and the absolute @NODE_BIN@
# below makes node itself the MainPID.
#
# WHY @NODE_BIN@ IS AN ABSOLUTE PATH THE INSTALLER READ OFF THIS VERY UNIT: it is the
# node the gateway is running now, not whatever node comes first on PATH — on a box
# whose system node is older than the version this repo declares, a PATH lookup would
# pin a binary that cannot load the gateway. The script path stays relative, so it
# resolves inside the unit's own WorkingDirectory and nowhere else.
[Unit]
Wants=crow-report-readers.socket
After=crow-report-readers.socket

[Service]
Sockets=crow-report-readers.socket
ExecStart=
ExecStart=@NODE_BIN@ servers/gateway/index.js